SUMMARY:UNRECYCLABLE:  Look Again - Assemblage Art Exhibit Opening
DESCRIPTION:UNRECYCLABLE: Look Again – Assemblage Art by Andrew Borg \nOpening Reception:  Friday\, August 14\, 5 – 8pm \nThe Space presents Unrecyclable: Look Again\, a solo exhibition of assemblage art by Andrew Borg composed predominantly of the unrecyclable plastics\, foams\, and composites he refused to throw away for nearly two years — the molded trays\, caps\, and packaging inserts that carry no recycling code and vanish into the trash without a thought. The exhibition\, culminating Borg’s year as Artist in Residence at The Space\, is on view August 14–22\, 2026\, with an opening reception Friday\, August 14\, from 5 to 8pm. \nWhat began as an act of defiance gradually became an act of appreciation: these are highly engineered\, purpose-built objects\, molded to cushion\, position\, and protect — aesthetic objects in their own right\, designed by someone\, meant to be forgotten by everyone. \nThe assemblage artworks in Unrecyclable: Look Again are composed from that two-year collection. The work asks viewers to make a conscious choice to look again — at the craft embedded in what we discard\, and at our own constant contributions to a stream of toxic materials that will outlast us by generations. \n“I collected these objects for almost two years before I fully understood why. Refusing to throw them away began as an act of defiance. Over time\, it became an obsession\, to look at them as raw material for re-expression — aesthetic objects with a conscience\,” says Borg. \nIn keeping with Montclair’s participatory community spirit\, the public is invited to create their own assemblage artworks during the opening reception\, using unrecyclable materials and art supplies provided by the gallery. \nThe exhibition closes with a Gallery Talk & Assemblage Lab on Saturday\, August 22\, 1–3pm. Borg gives a gallery talk\, then leads a hands-on session in which participants re-see “ghost objects” — abandoned electronics and appliances — and combine them with other unrecyclable materials to build assemblages of their own. All materials provided; no prior artistic experience required.  Register here. \nBorg was invited to mount the exhibition by The Space founder Naz Botas\, following his year in residence. \nAbout the Artist: Andrew Borg is an assemblage artist and 2025–26 Artist in Residence at The Space in Montclair\, NJ. Trained in painting at Harvard\, he danced professionally in NYC for nine years\, then spent four decades in technology innovation. His current series asks us to look again at what we throw away.
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/unrecyclable-look-again-assemblage-art-by-andrew-borg/
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-29-at-2.48.27-PM.png
END:VEVENT
