SUMMARY:Assemblage Lab & Gallery Talk with Andrew Borg
DESCRIPTION:Assemblage Lab & Gallery Talk with Andrew Borg\nClosing Event for “Unrecyclable: Look Again” \nWhat do you see when you really look at what you throw away? \nJoin artist Andrew Borg for the closing event of Unrecyclable: Look Again — an afternoon that begins with a gallery talk and ends with your hands deep in materials you never thought twice about discarding. \nAfter walking through the exhibition and sharing the story behind his two-year collection of unrecyclable plastics\, foams\, and composites\, Borg leads an immersive hands-on Assemblage Lab in which participants get to experience the process firsthand. Using unrecyclable packaging\, abandoned electronics\, appliances\, and other “ghost objects\,” you’ll build your own assemblage\, sculpture\, or mixed-media artwork — guided by the same impulse that drove this exhibition: look again. \nNo artistic experience required. No right or wrong. Just a fresh set of eyes and a willingness to see the overlooked as raw material for something new. \nUnrecyclable materials are provided\, along with glue to put your assemblages together. Bring your own materials too — packaging\, foam inserts\, bottle caps\, old electronics\, anything you’ve been meaning to throw away. The stranger the better. \n🗓 Saturday\, August 22 | 1:00 pm – 3:00 pm\n📍 The Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, 2nd Floor\, Montclair\, NJ\n🎟 $10 \nPart gallery talk\, part art lab\, all creative. Come ready to make something!
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/assemblage-lab-gallery-talk-with-andrew-borg/
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-29-at-2.48.27-PM.png
END:VEVENT
